static const unsigned char app_apps_README_md[] =
    "# cwick apps\n\nEach app is a self-contained H5 bundle und"
    "er `apps/<id>/`; `manifest.json`\nlists what the built-in"
    " app market shows. The server embeds this tree into the\n"
    "binary (see `tools/embed_web.c`) and serves it at `/apps"
    "/...` on the same\norigin as the OpenAI API, so an app ne"
    "eds no build step, no package manager and\nno CORS config"
    "uration.\n\nLayout:\n\n```\napps/\n  manifest.json          # "
    "the market catalog\n  tictactoe/             # \344\271\235\345\256\253\346\240\274\344"
    "\272\225\345\255\227\346\243\213\n    app.json             # app metadata (kept n"
    "ext to the code)\n    index.html           # entry\n    ap"
    "p.css\n    app.js\n  kart/                  # 3D \346\263\241\346\263\241\345\215\241"
    "\344\270\201\350\275\246\n    app.json\n    index.html\n    app.css\n    app.j"
    "s\n  imagegen/              # H5 \345\233\276\345\203\217\347\224\237\346\210\220\n    app.jso"
    "n\n    index.html\n    app.css\n    app.js\n```\n\nThe decisio"
    "n apps (tictactoe, kart) ask the model through `POST /v1"
    "/systemone`;\n`imagegen` calls the image endpoints `/v1/i"
    "mages/edits` and\n`/v1/images/generations` instead. The c"
    "hat tab keeps using\n`/v1/chat/completions`. Every reques"
    "t an app makes is same-origin \342\200\224\nthere is no configurab"
    "le external endpoint. The resident model is discovered\nf"
    "rom `GET /v1/models` and re-discovered after a server-si"
    "de switch, so the\ndecision adapter always follows the ch"
    "eckpoint that is actually loaded.\n\nTo add an app: create"
    " `apps/<id>/`, add its entry to `manifest.json`, then ru"
    "n\n`make` (which builds and runs the C generator `tools/e"
    "mbed_web`) and restart\n`cwick serve --web`.\n\n## Where an"
    " app keeps its data\n\n**Not** in `localStorage` alone. Th"
    "e server owns the databases in `~/.cwick/apps/`\n(`--stor"
    "e DIR`, or `$CWICK_STORE`): **one file per app**, `<id>."
    "db`, plus `auth.db`\nfor the server's own API keys. A `--"
    "store` path that exists as a file or ends in\n`.db`/`.sql"
    "ite` still means one shared database \342\200\224 the old layout "
    "\342\200\224 and every\napp's rows then live in that one file behi"
    "nd their `app_id`.\n\nRun from a checkout, `--store ./apps"
    "` puts each app's database right next to its\ncode (`apps"
    "/tictactoe.db`, `apps/kart.db`). That is deliberate and "
    "safe:\n`tools/embed_web.c` skips every database suffix wh"
    "en it walks `apps/`, so a\nrunning server's files are nev"
    "er compiled into the binary, and `.gitignore`\nkeeps them"
    " out of a commit.\n\nThree generic collections per app, al"
    "l behind the same login as the model:\n\n```\nGET    /v1/st"
    "ore                          layout, per-app row counts,"
    " file size\nGET    /v1/store?app=<id>                 tha"
    "t app's own database\nGET    /v1/apps/<id>/state         "
    "       every key            -> {\"items\":[...]}\nGET    /v"
    "1/apps/<id>/state?key=K          one value            ->"
    " {\"value\":<json>}\nPUT    /v1/apps/<id>/state            "
    "    {\"key\":K,\"value\":V} or {\"values\":{...}}\nDELETE /v1/a"
    "pps/<id>/state?key=K\nGET    /v1/apps/<id>/events?game_id"
    "=G&limit=N\nPOST   /v1/apps/<id>/events               {\"g"
    "ame_id\",\"seq\",\"kind\",\"payload\"}\nGET    /v1/apps/<id>/gam"
    "es?limit=N        newest first\nPUT    /v1/apps/<id>/game"
    "s                {\"game_id\",\"started_at\",\"ended_at\",\"out"
    "come\",\"moves\"}\nDELETE /v1/apps/<id>/games?game_id=G     "
    " the game and its events\n```\n\nEvery value and payload mu"
    "st be JSON; it is stored as the exact text that\narrived "
    "and handed back verbatim, so an app never has to match a"
    " schema the\nserver invented. `<id>` is `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,"
    "64}` \342\200\224 checked before it reaches\nsqlite \342\200\224 and limits"
    " are 1 MiB per value / payload and 5000 rows per read.\n\n"
    "Why a server-side store rather than `localStorage`:\n\n- \""
    "clear site data\", a private window or a second browser p"
    "rofile would erase a\n  match history the model produced;"
    "\n- the phone that scanned the QR is a different browser "
    "and must see the same\n  scoreboard and history;\n- an app"
    "'s history is worth keeping after the tab is gone.\n\n`app"
    "s/tictactoe` uses all three collections: `state` for the"
    " scoreboard, `games`\nfor one row per match (`started_at`"
    ", `ended_at`, `outcome`, `moves`) and\n`events` for one r"
    "ow per move (`kind` = `human`/`ai`, payload = board snap"
    "shot,\nprompt with the per-cell tactical facts, the model"
    "'s full probability\ndistribution as `probs`, raw model a"
    "nswer, parsed move, latency, usage). The\nright-hand colu"
    "mn's **\345\216\206\345\217\262\345\233\236\346\224\276** tab reads them back and replays a "
    "finished game\nstep by step.\n\n`apps/kart` uses the same t"
    "hree: `games` for one row per run (`moves` = obstacles\nt"
    "he model placed), `events` for `kind` = `spawn`/`hit`/`l"
    "ap`/`end` (payload = the\nobstacle type, the position on "
    "the strip, the kart's speed, the model's latency,\nits ra"
    "w answer, plus the variation `seed`, pressure `focus` an"
    "d decision\n`entropy`) and `state` for the best score and"
    " a lifetime tally. Every spawn is a\nmodel decision, so t"
    "he replay shows what the model actually said for each\nob"
    "stacle rather than a number from a generator.\n\n## Which "
    "apps decide, and through which endpoint\n\nBoth hosted app"
    "s ask the model to choose, and both call `POST /v1/syste"
    "mone`.\nThe chat tab is a different consumer: it uses `/v"
    "1/chat/completions`, because a\nconversation is generated"
    " text, not a choice among options.\n\n- **tic-tac-toe** \342\200"
    "\224 the human plays X first. Each machine move is a `choic"
    "e`\n  over the empty cells, and the question is explicitl"
    "y *which cell gives O the\n  greatest probability of winn"
    "ing*. The state carries the board and one line of\n  tact"
    "ical facts per empty cell (immediate win, forced block, "
    "winning replies,\n  open lines). Those are facts, not a r"
    "anked list: the old wording \342\200\224 \"win, else\n  block, else"
    " centre, else corner\" \342\200\224 was a local rule dressed up as"
    " a question\n  and was removed. `fallbackMove()` remains,"
    " but only for a failed request.\n- **kart** \342\200\224 a 12-way "
    "`choice` of obstacle kind and lane, asked in real time\n "
    " while the kart is moving. The question now asks for *ma"
    "ximum difficulty*; the\n  previous \"leave room for the pl"
    "ayer to react\" was the opposite of the goal.\n\nWhat stays"
    " local is what a letter cannot express: the kart's obsta"
    "cle distance\nis derived from speed (and tightens with th"
    "e lap, above a reaction floor). The\nmodel decides *what*"
    ", the app computes *where* \342\200\224 and an app never substitu"
    "tes a\nlocally generated obstacle for a model decision.\n\n"
    "Any app that caches a model id must handle a switch on t"
    "he server side: a 400\nwhose text says the model is no lo"
    "nger served drops the cached id, rediscovers\nthe residen"
    "t model and retries once. `GET /v1/systemone` answers wh"
    "ich family,\nprompt grammar and letter set are live, so a"
    " client can check rather than\ninfer.\n\n## The win-probabi"
    "lity readout in `apps/tictactoe`\n\n`cellFacts()` computes"
    ", for each empty cell and each mark, whether the move\nwi"
    "ns immediately, whether it blocks the opponent's immedia"
    "te win, how many\nwinning replies remain, and how many li"
    "nes are still open. It never ranks or\npicks a cell \342\200\224 i"
    "t is the same information a human counts, rendered into "
    "the\nstate and into each option's description. The endpoi"
    "nt's softmax over the\noption letters is the model's dist"
    "ribution over \"which cell wins most\"; its\nargmax is the "
    "move.\n\nThe right-hand column draws one bar per empty cel"
    "l, highlights the cell\nactually played, and shows the hu"
    "man's own tactical facts on their move, so\nboth sides of"
    " the game have a decision trail. The bars are a readout "
    "of one\nprefill, **not** a Monte-Carlo win rate, and the "
    "heading says so: calling them\na simulated win percentage"
    " would be a claim the endpoint cannot make.\n\n## The mode"
    "l decides the obstacles in `apps/kart`\n\n`pumpAgent()` ru"
    "ns once per frame while racing and keeps at most one req"
    "uest in\nflight and a two-deep queue of decisions, becaus"
    "e a kart covers ~13 m in the\ntime a 320B model takes to "
    "answer \342\200\224 so the model is asked about a stretch of\ntrac"
    "k 45\342\200\22395 m ahead rather than about the next frame.\n\nThe"
    " question is a 12-way `choice` at `/v1/systemone`: four "
    "obstacle kinds times\nthree lanes, one letter each. The m"
    "odel never writes a lane offset or a\ndistance \342\200\224 number"
    "s it would have to generate token by token, and then be\n"
    "repaired when it wrote prose around them. The distance i"
    "s derived locally from\nthe kart's speed, which also keep"
    "s the road readable: the player sees where the\nthing wil"
    "l be, not just what kind it is. The state is one line of"
    " English facts: lap, speed, hits, obstacles ahead,\nspawn"
    "ed so far, difficulty level, which side of the strip is "
    "up, a variation\nseed and a pressure point. Every byte is"
    " prefill on every obstacle, which is\nwhy the option labe"
    "ls are short English and the Chinese names stay in the\ns"
    "idebar.\n\n**Real-time random decisions.** The readout is "
    "deterministic for a fixed\nprompt, and a fixed A..L order"
    " would put the model's letter bias on the same\nobstacle "
    "every time. Each request therefore Fisher-Yates shuffles"
    " the twelve\noptions (`criteria` is an ordered object on "
    "the server, so member order becomes\nthe letters), draws "
    "a fresh variation seed and one of six pressure points, a"
    "nd\nasks for the hardest obstacle it can choose. The vari"
    "ation lives in the\n*question*, never on the road: the se"
    "ed, pressure point and the normalised\nentropy of the res"
    "ulting distribution are shown in the sidebar and written"
    " to\nthe sqlite `agent`/`spawn` events, so it is auditabl"
    "e rather than hidden.\n\n**There is no local generator beh"
    "ind it.** This is the requirement, not an\naccident: an e"
    "mpty queue means an empty road, the HUD says `\346\250\241\345\236\213\347\246\273\347"
    "\272\277 \302\267 \346\232\202\344\270\215\346\224\276\350\267\257\351\232\234`,\nand the sidebar's `\345\267\262\346\224\276\350\267\257\351\232\234`"
    " can never exceed the model's successful decisions.\nThe "
    "alternative \342\200\224 silently inventing obstacles when the mo"
    "del is slow \342\200\224 makes\nthe statistics a lie and hides a b"
    "roken integration behind a playable game.\n\nThree traps t"
    "his app has already hit, all worth remembering:\n\n- the m"
    "odel id must be the one the server advertises (`GET /v1/"
    "models`), never a\n  literal \342\200\224 an invented name is a 40"
    "0 and the model is never asked at all;\n- `ensureModel()`"
    " returns the discovery promise from `resolveModel()`, wh"
    "ich\n  caches the in-flight `GET /v1/models` so several o"
    "bstacles spawned in one\n  frame share a single lookup. A"
    "n empty answer must not be cached, or one cold\n  start w"
    "ould leave the game without obstacles for the whole run."
    " Failures like\n  that are invisible on screen \342\200\224 the ro"
    "ad is just empty for a moment \342\200\224 so the\n  model state i"
    "s exposed under `?debug`;\n- a model id cached before a s"
    "erver-side switch is refused on *every* call\n  (\"model `"
    "x` is not served by this endpoint\"). A 400 with that tex"
    "t now drops\n  the id, rediscovers the resident model and"
    " retries once;\n- one decision is one prefill, and the en"
    "dpoint takes a generation slot: on this\n  single-slot se"
    "rver an obstacle decision queues behind a chat turn. Tha"
    "t is why\n  the queue is only two deep and why an empty q"
    "ueue is shown as an empty road\n  rather than papered ove"
    "r.\n\n## The 3D renderer in `apps/kart`\n\nNo WebGL, no libr"
    "ary: the kart is a small triangle rasteriser on a 2D can"
    "vas.\nEach frame it pushes ~700 triangles into one buffer"
    " (track quads, curbs, centre\nand edge lines, quarter-lap"
    " gates, obstacle boxes, the kart), sorts them\nfar-to-nea"
    "r and fills them. Three details carry the whole thing:\n\n"
    "- **camera space is forward-positive.** `toCam()` dots a"
    " point with (right, up,\n  forward) from the eye, so z > "
    "0 means in front; the projection divides by z and\n  a Su"
    "therland\342\200\223Hodgman clip against `z >= NEAR` trims the po"
    "lygons that straddle\n  the camera. An earlier version us"
    "ed the OpenGL convention (forward = \342\210\222z) in the\n  view "
    "matrix while the clip assumed +z, which culled the entir"
    "e world;\n- **normals are normalised before shading.** Th"
    "e cross product of a quad's edges\n  has length = its are"
    "a (a road segment is 8.8 m by 1.7 m, so |n| \342\211\210 15); usi"
    "ng\n  that directly as a brightness factor saturates ever"
    "y large quad to white,\n  which is exactly how one build "
    "turned the strip into a white slab;\n- **the camera's up "
    "vector is the surface normal**, so the horizon rolls wit"
    "h the\n  strip instead of staying level with the world. T"
    "hat is what makes the flip\n  readable rather than a floa"
    "ting camera over a twisted ribbon;\n- **road texture must"
    " be indexed by world position, not by segment index.** T"
    "he\n  banding and centre dashes were picked with `i & 1` "
    "over the window the camera\n  draws; because that window "
    "moves with the kart, the pattern moved with it and\n  the"
    " road looked painted on the lens \342\200\224 93 km/h and nothing"
    " on the surface said\n  so. Snapping the segments to a wo"
    "rld grid (`first = floor(u / du)`) makes the\n  stripes s"
    "tream past. A chase cam also needs a spring: with the ey"
    "e an exact\n  function of the kart's position, accelerati"
    "on shows nothing; a few metres of\n  lag, a 2 cm bob and "
    "a focal kick with speed are what \"driving\" looks like.\n\n"
    "The track is a parametric M\303\266bius strip, `S(u, v) = C(u)"
    " + A(u)\302\267v` with\n`A(u) = cos(u/2)\302\267radial + sin(u/2)\302\267up"
    "`, so after one lap the across direction is\nreversed \342\200\224"
    " one side, one surface, and the gates built in that fram"
    "e arrive\nupside down half a lap later.\n\nThe strip is dra"
    "wn in two zones: the near ~1.3 rad at full detail (bandi"
    "ng,\nkerbs, dashes, painted start/twist bands) and the re"
    "st out to 4.4 rad as one\ncoarse quad per 0.08 rad plus a"
    " bright rim. Without the far zone a M\303\266bius track\nis ind"
    "istinguishable from a banked ring \342\200\224 you only ever see "
    "the ten metres under\nthe kart. The rim is what carries t"
    "he shape: a M\303\266bius strip is recognised by its\nsingle co"
    "ntinuous edge.\n\nA chase camera sits *inside* the twist, "
    "which is exactly why the app also draws a\nsmall inset: t"
    "he whole loop from outside the ring, with up-facing face"
    "s teal and\ndown-facing faces violet so the half-twist sh"
    "ows as a colour flip, plus the\nkart's dot. Its projectio"
    "n is written separately from the main camera on\npurpose "
    "\342\200\224 the main camera is a per-frame function of the kart "
    "and must not be\ndisturbed by a 140-pixel diagram. `?debu"
    "g` exposes `window.__kart` (`G`, `AGENT`,\n`tris()`, `fra"
    "meAt`) so a headless run can tell \"zero triangles\" from "
    "\"triangles\nbehind the camera\".\n\n## Sharing on the LAN\n\n`"
    "cwick serve --lan` binds all interfaces (no auth/TLS; tr"
    "usted Wi-Fi only) and\nprints e.g. `LAN share: http://192"
    ".168.71.84:8001/apps/tictactoe/`. **Every app\nhere carri"
    "es a \345\210\206\344\272\253 / \344\272\214\347\273\264\347\240\201 button** \342\200\224 it calls `GET /v1/s"
    "hare?app=<id>` and\nrenders the answer through `GET /v1/s"
    "hare/qr?text=<url>`; scanning the PNG opens\nthat app sta"
    "ndalone on a phone. Two things are worth knowing:\n\n- **t"
    "he `?app=` is not optional for a new app.** The server's"
    " default is\n  `tictactoe`, so an app that forgets it wil"
    "l happily hand out a QR for somebody\n  else's page. The "
    "id is charset-checked before it reaches `printf`.\n- **`s"
    "hareable:false` is a real answer**, returned with a `war"
    "ning` when the\n  listener is loopback-only or has no LAN"
    " IPv4. The sheet shows the reason and\n  the `--lan` hint"
    " instead of a code that would not resolve.\n\n\nWith `--lan"
    "`, cwick forces single-user login, so an unauthenticated"
    " phone is\nredirected to `/login?next=/apps/<id>/` and re"
    "turns to the app after the\npassword \342\200\224 which is why eve"
    "ry share note says the first open needs it. The apps\nare"
    " responsive (tested at 390 px) and do not need the main "
    "console shell when\nopened from that URL \342\200\224 the kart ope"
    "ns straight into its race because that is all\nit does.\n"
    "\000";

